Software Foundation — release order

1. Choose an immutable source revision, version and complete asset matrix.
2. Confirm dependency terms, pinned sources, notices, SDK recipe and target policy.
3. Complete applicable regression, backend, platform and ABI checks for that source.
4. Build each configuration once; package the resulting binaries. Never move a
   configured build tree between hosts. Preserve source and dependency inputs.
5. Inventory each final archive and verify that exact archive after relocation:
   python3 tools/artifact.py create ARCHIVE --manifest MANIFEST.json
   python3 tools/artifact.py verify ARCHIVE --manifest MANIFEST.json
6. Populate docs/templates/release-manifest.json and attach actual evidence,
   source identity, runtime floor, notices, checksums and remaining omissions.
7. Stage immutable release assets. Verify downloads and inventories before making
   the release generally available. Never replace published bytes under one name.
8. Publish package-repository metadata only after packages exist and verify fully.
   GitHub download assets alone do not constitute an APT repository.
9. Certify the exact published artifacts, retain reports, and promote only when
   all required gates pass. A diagnostic or incomplete run cannot qualify them.

This repository supplies native archive examples and a release specification.
It does not include credentials, remote publishing, a compiled cross SDK, or a
qualified older-runtime release. See docs/releases.md and docs/validation.md.
